Table 3 - Empirical validation against known_data, C-engine run (Analysis C)
============================================================================

Run: SIMULATION_20261012_205659 (C engine, model key c_engine). Reference: WEB_DEVEL/data/known_data, used as is.
Pre-specified definitions (the same as AAA_TEST/sim_comparison, fixed before any comparison):
  empirical acceptance: Bhattacharyya coefficient >= 0.97 (project rule, data_extractor.py)
  empirical W1 tolerance: 2.0 passengers
  operational issue rule: P(O >= 60) >= 0.1; crowding threshold 60 of capacity 80
  peak slots: (7, 8, 9, 17, 18, 19); bootstrap: resamples of complete replicas, seed 20261013

Calibration-period validation: the reference is a fitted normal of the same operational records that calibrate the inputs.

